{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["Because Scripture said <b>such as has not been in Egypt since the day it was founded</b>, and then repeated and said further (Exodus 9:24), \"very heavy, such as had not been like it in all the land of Egypt since it became a nation,\" it hints that there are other places in the world upon which the like has come down, similar to the matter of \"YHWH cast down upon them great stones from heaven\" (Joshua 10:11), or similar to the matter of Sodom — sulfur and salt and fire — but in the land of Egypt, where the rains do not fall and neither does hail, this was a great wonder in it. And I have not understood what is said in Bereshit Rabbah (Shemot Rabbah 12:3): it does not say 'such as had not been in Egypt like it' but rather 'such as had not been like it in Egypt' — meaning there was nothing like it in the world and not in Egypt. And the meaning of <b>since the day it was founded</b> is as if to say: your fathers and the fathers of your fathers never saw the like in it from eternity. And it is impossible to say that the like occurred before the world was founded, or before the earth became a nation. And perhaps, because this hail is a punishment for the sin of its inhabitants and is not in the normal course of the world, Scripture may say so — that the like did not come in the iniquities of their fathers — for before it became a nation, it is a clear matter that the like did not come." "<b>Behold, I will cause it to rain hail tomorrow at this time — now therefore send, gather in</b> — all these are the words of YHWH to Moses, and it is known that Moses came and said to Pharaoh all the words of YHWH that He sent him, and there was no need to elaborate, so Scripture only said, 'he who fears the word of YHWH' — for Moses had spoken thus to them. And this counsel was in the compassion of YHWH, for the plague of hail He sent only to destroy the produce of the land, and not upon the people; therefore He points out the sinners a way to save themselves from it."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The citation 'בראשית רבה' is resolved as Shemot Rabbah 12:3 per the parenthetical reference given in the source text."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:05:09.380874109Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}